  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-30T08:27:02.563Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A toggle in the hand menu that will immobilize your avatar's legs/hips as they would when browsing the main menu. This is particularly handy for half body players who don't want their legs swinging around them when they move their head while crouching and proning. This was a mod before EAC and I knew a ton of people that had it. It was a must-have in the QoL modding scene for half body players. There are ways to make this work on avatars with a Unity plugin called Gogo Loco, but it's clunky and hard to get working, not to mention resource-intensive as far as performance.  I don't think it's right to expect people to know how to use Unity just to freeze the lower half of their avatars when they wanna cuddle or take photos. I know Quest users specifically hunt down public avatars with Gogo Loco on it just for the opportunity to freeze their avatars, so I think it would be a great addition for all half body players, regardless of VRC platform.",
